# Evidence Review Workspace — manual API walkthrough
#
# Works with the VS Code "REST Client" extension and JetBrains HTTP Client.
# Run the requests top to bottom; later requests reuse values captured from
# earlier responses. Postman users: import the equivalent curl commands from
# scripts/demo_flow.sh, or follow docs/api.md.
#
# Start the API first:  cd backend && .venv/bin/uvicorn app.main:create_app --factory --reload

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8000

### 1. Health check — expect {"status":"ok","database":"connected"}
GET {{baseUrl}}/health

### 2. Create (or load) the seeded demo. 201 the first time, 200 afterwards.
#    Add ?reset=true to delete and recreate it (clears saved reviews).
# @name demo
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/demo

@projectId = {{demo.response.body.project_id}}
@draftId = {{demo.response.body.draft_id}}

### 3. Fetch the demo project
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/projects/{{projectId}}

### 4. Fetch all claims (composite: source, evidence, latest AI assessment, review)
# @name claims
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/drafts/{{draftId}}/claims

@claim1 = {{claims.response.body.claims[0].id}}
@claim2 = {{claims.response.body.claims[1].id}}
@claim3 = {{claims.response.body.claims[2].id}}

### 5. Fetch one claim (the mortality figure mismatch)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/claims/{{claim2}}

### 6. KEEP the supported hospitalization claim
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/claims/{{claim1}}/review
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "decision": "KEEP",
  "reviewer_note": "Figure, outcome and comparator match the abstract (OR 0.78, 95% CI 0.70–0.87)."
}

### 7. QUALIFY the mortality claim, with revised wording
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/claims/{{claim2}}/review
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "decision": "QUALIFY",
  "reviewer_note": "Changed 22% to 19% and retained odds terminology.",
  "revised_claim": "Non-invasive remote patient monitoring was associated with approximately 19% lower odds of death compared with usual care (pooled OR 0.81, 95% CI 0.69–0.95)."
}

### 8. REMOVE the overgeneralized claim
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/claims/{{claim3}}/review
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "decision": "REMOVE",
  "reviewer_note": "Pooled trial estimates do not support benefit for every patient."
}

### 8b. Validation example — REPLACE without revised_claim returns 422
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/claims/{{claim1}}/review
Content-Type: application/json

{ "decision": "REPLACE" }

### 9. Progress — expect reviewed_claims 3 of 3, is_complete true
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/projects/{{projectId}}/progress

### 10. Export JSON (structured issues and review history)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/projects/{{projectId}}/export?format=json

### 11. Export CSV
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/projects/{{projectId}}/export?format=csv

### 12. Verify persistence — the decisions are still there on a fresh read
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/projects/{{projectId}}/audit

#######################################################################
# Phase 3 — AI pipeline
# With LLM_PROVIDER=groq these requests use your Groq quota:
# analyze ≈ 1 + (number of claims) calls; reassess = 1 call.
#######################################################################

### 13. New project for a live analysis
# @name p3project
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/projects
Content-Type: application/json

{ "title": "Heart-failure RPM — live analysis" }

@p3ProjectId = {{p3project.response.body.id}}

### 14. Paste a draft with a numbered reference list
# @name p3draft
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/projects/{{p3ProjectId}}/drafts
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "original_text": "Non-invasive remote patient monitoring (RPM) was associated with lower odds of first heart-failure hospitalization compared with usual care (pooled OR 0.78) [1]. It lowered the odds of death by 22% [1]. It works for every heart-failure patient [1].\n\n[1] De Lathauwer ILJ, Nieuwenhuys WW, Hafkamp F, et al. Remote patient monitoring in heart failure: a comprehensive meta-analysis of effective programme components for hospitalization and mortality reduction. Eur J Heart Fail. 2025;27(9):1670-1685. doi:10.1002/ejhf.3568"
}

@p3DraftId = {{p3draft.response.body.id}}

### 15. Analyze (synchronous: extraction → DOI resolution → evidence → assessment)
#    Add {"refresh_metadata": true} to bypass the DOI cache and hit Crossref/OpenAlex.
# @name analysis
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/drafts/{{p3DraftId}}/analyze
Content-Type: application/json

{}

@p3Claim = {{analysis.response.body.claims[1].id}}

### 16. Analyze again — expect rerun=true, claims_reused=N, llm_calls=0
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/drafts/{{p3DraftId}}/analyze

### 17. Re-assess one claim (appends a new assessment; reviews are kept)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/claims/{{p3Claim}}/assess
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### 18. Explicit marker → DOI mapping (overrides the reference list)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/drafts/{{p3DraftId}}/analyze
Content-Type: application/json

{ "citations": { "1": "10.1002/ejhf.3568" } }

### 19. Re-extract (409 reviews_exist once any claim has a human decision)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/drafts/{{p3DraftId}}/analyze
Content-Type: application/json

{ "mode": "reextract" }
